info
# Issue #1933: the batched GraphQL issue-state query (are_issues_open)
# partially failed -- a per-node `Could not resolve` error left some issue
# numbers unresolved, and the parallel per-issue `issue_view` fallback ran
# for exactly those numbers instead of the whole batch. The payload names
# the unresolved numbers (the telemetry the incident lacked).
# Edge-triggered per number and durable across passes (issue #2901): the
# baseline of already-reported numbers is a per-repo sidecar next to
# state.json (github_capabilities/unresolved_issue_baseline.py), so a
# persistent stale blocker emits ONE row, not one per pass -- the fleet
# supervisor rebuilds its GitHub client every pass, which is why the earlier
# instance-local baseline re-reported it every pass (2,081 rows/week in one
# consumer repo). A number re-emits only after a later batch positively
# resolves it and it then goes stale again. If the sidecar cannot be written
# the client falls back to the instance-local baseline, whose per-pass repeat
# is the flood shape #1271/#1768 burned check_warning_events with once.
# Info, not warning: this records a degradation that the per-issue fallback
# already absorbed (the answer is still correct), so it must not alarm.
